WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Today I'm recording how to assemble the Freak Mech Blade armour-opening spinner.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
First, let's take it apart.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
This is the lock. I've already unscrewed it.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then just undo the screws on the body.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
We'll take it all apart first, then show how to put it together.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
This second body half is held on by magnets, so just prise it off.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Work along one edge.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
This is one of the body halves.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The armour plates are magnetic too. Just lift them off.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
When you take it apart, you'll find lots of beads.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
I'll explain how to fit the beads when I put it back together.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Once it's apart, lay the parts out.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
I'm demonstrating, so I've taken it apart completely.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
When you're changing to a DIY mode, you don't need to strip it this far.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Roughly sorted: these are the armour plates.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
These are the rods, and these are the blades.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The lock, and the two body halves.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The hardest part of taking it apart and rebuilding it is the body.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The beads are hard to control.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Our fix is the lubricating oil that comes in the box.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The oil holds the beads in their slots,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
so even upside down, the beads won't fall out.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
This one I've already done.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
So how do you do it? I'll use this half to show you.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Take the lubricating oil and pick a container.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
A small dish like this, or even a small bottle cap, works.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Drip the oil in. A drop or two is basically enough.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then soak the beads in it,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
so each bead is coated in oil.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Once they're coated, put them straight in.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Another way, if you don't have a container:

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
put the oil on a cotton bud,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
then wipe the cotton bud round the holes,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
so there's a little oil in each hole.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then press the beads in. It works the same way.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
That's the beads done on both body halves.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Next, fit the armour plates.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The plates are magnetic. Just let them snap on.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
If you fit one the wrong way round, it won't stick.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
That's the three armour plates fitted.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
With the three plates on, fit the blades.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
When you're putting it together, always check

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
there's a bead in each of the three bead slots.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Beginners can easily leave these beads out.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The blades can go either way up.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Just let them snap on.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Make sure all three are the same.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
There's a round hole left in each,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
so you can add magnets later.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Point all three the same way,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
then put them in.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
That's the three blades in.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Now we're assembling the single rods.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
If you want the crisp single-rod armour-opening mode,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
just assemble it like this.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The holes for the rods are already made.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Follow this direction and fit them in order.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
This part isn't difficult.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Good, that's the single rods fitted.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Next, take the other body half

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
and put it back on, face down.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
It snaps on with the magnets.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
One thing to watch:

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
when you're putting it together,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
always fix the beads in place first,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
so they don't move about.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then it's very easy to put together.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The beads in both body halves

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
must already be held in with the oil

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
before you put it together.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then we put it on, like this.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
A quick press and it's in.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
That's the single rods assembled.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Put the screws straight in,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:22.500 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
then tighten the lock,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
and single-rod mode is ready.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Now flip it over

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
and prise the other side open again.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
See, the beads are all held firmly in place.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
They won't fall out,

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
which makes it very easy.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Hang on, I'll grab the rods from over there.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
These are the rods for the other side.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
The process is the same.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Prise it open,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
then fit the rods in order.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Some people like to use tweezers.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
It depends what you're used to.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Do whatever's comfortable.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Same again: once these rods are fitted,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
snap the body half back on.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then we can put the screws back in

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
and test it.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Don't tighten the lock yet.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Open it first,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
to make sure no beads have dropped out

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
and that it opens smoothly.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
That shows the assembly has worked.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Then just tighten the lock.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
When you're tightening the lock,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
check the post isn't bent.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
Keep the post straight.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.000 line:6% position:50% size:92% align:center
And that's it, all assembled.
